WEBVTT

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.390
Finally.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.890
Yeah.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:41.810
Yes.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.420
By the way, gramps, don't you have to shave your beard?

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.520
It's all right.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.860
We're a bit different from other cake shops.

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:54.690
But...

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.860
it's raining.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.620
With this rain, there won't be many customers.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:03.700
Tachibana says jiu (慈雨), welcome rain, but Eiji hears jiyu (自由), freedom.
It's a beneficial rain.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:04.310
Tachibana says jiu (慈雨), welcome rain, but Eiji hears jiyu (自由), freedom.

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:05.270
Freedom?

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:07.330
Tachibana says jiu (慈雨), welcome rain, but Eiji hears jiyu (自由), freedom.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.290
It's a welcome rain.

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:17.560
Antique, open for business!

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:55.380
And...

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.990
why are you two still here?

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:01.340
Well, we've done what we had to do...

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.870
...and we're at loose ends.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:06.090
What about you, Tachibana?

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:08.470
Have you mastered the information about the cakes?

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:11.290
You didn't really taste any of them till today.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:14.920
It'll be a problem if you can't sell sensei's cakes.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:20.540
Are you guys saying that to me,
the best salesman at my former company?

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:21.300
A customer.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:22.520
Welcome.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:23.890
Oh.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:27.890
So the antique shop failed, and a cake shop opened in its place?

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:30.920
Let's see what you can do, gramps.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:35.770
Welcome, Madam.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.740
Are you looking for a present?

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:42.510
Y-Yeah.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.420
What would you recommend?

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:46.580
I've been invited to a tea party.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:49.800
Then, how about these crèmes?

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:53.710
An assortment of three kinds of custards, filled with whipped cream.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:57.220
Custards go well with any type of tea,

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:59.270
and they're also easy to carry.

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:01.130
Then may I have them?

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.450
Of course, Madam.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.260
Thank you for waiting.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.900
Please enjoy your tea party.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:16.270
These cakes will add grace to, and enhance the pleasure of, your experience.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:19.200
I'm glad that such a nice shop opened.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.570
Thank you very much.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.240
Gramps is great at this.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:23.990
Yeah.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:27.370
Wow! Everything looks tasty. I can't decide.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:31.080
Then, how about this President?

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:37.890
It's our original rare cheese cake, made with the richly flavored French cream cheese "President."

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:42.760
A sweet-and-sour raspberry sponge cake, and a framboise topping, serve to accent the flavor.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.630
I recommend this one for ladies.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:46.720
Then I'll take it.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.890
Me too.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.890
Thank you very much.

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:52.810
I want something to take as a present to my client.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.860
I see.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:57.550
What about this Saint Marc?

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.410
It's a chocolate confection, filled with whipped cream,

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:04.700
flavored with kirsch and chocolate mousse, giving it a rich, gorgeous taste.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:09.320
I would really like adults to give this cake a try.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:10.950
How do you like it?

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.230
I see. It sounds really delicious.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.600
Then, can I have twenty?

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.290
Thank you very much.

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:22.500
We await your next visit.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:23.580
Thank you.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:27.750
Well, how was that?

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:30.400
You studied quite well in a very short time.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:32.250
Easy-peasy.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:38.810
Are you all right?

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:39.690
Damn it.

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.910
Why is that foreign car speeding like that?!

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:43.820
This is a speed-restricted road! I'm going to kick his ass!

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.470
Now, now. Tachibana.

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:48.660
A scary guy could be driving that kind of car.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.050
Oh...

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:53.140
It's coming back.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:55.410
I don't care. Get out of the car.

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:14.870
It's him!

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:16.250
This is bad.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.430
I finally left my parent's house, but now he's chasing me.

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:19.390
What is it?
I finally left my parent's house, but now he's chasing me.

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:21.070
Is he a debt collector?

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:54.180
Young master.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:55.600
Young master?

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:59.520
Waka (若) is young master; Eiji hears baka (馬鹿), idiot.
Idiot?

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.850
Hey, gramps...

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:14.860
What do you do, Tachibana?

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:19.620
You know a trading company called Shirai Products, right?

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:20.800
Yes.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:21.960
Nah.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.460
Then, what about Shirai Bank?

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.140
Sure, I know that.

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:27.060
Of course.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:28.550
It's the biggest city bank.

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:33.880
The chairman of the Shirai group is my maternal grandfather.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:35.220
What?

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:39.630
So Tachibana, you're the grandchild of the chairman of a conglomerate.

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:40.810
I see.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.620
But I'm not the only grandchild,

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:45.890
so I'm not going to inherit.

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:48.730
But young master was the best of all.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:52.760
Umm... I know it's rude, but are you Tachibana's...

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:53.350
A pun on Chikage's name: kage (影) means shadow.
Shadow.

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:54.410
No!
A pun on Chikage's name: kage (影) means shadow.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.390
It's Chikage. Chikage. Kobayakawa Chikage.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:59.690
He's just a housekeeper for my parents!

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:00.820
Just a...

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:02.080
...housekeeper?

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:04.910
Young master, that's harsh.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:06.510
Geez.

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:11.750
That's why I told them not to tell Chikage where I lived.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:13.440
Young master...

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:14.430
Eh? What?

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:20.470
I'm here because your mother and father earnestly requested it.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:30.360
I'll support you from the shadows from now on.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:31.650
Goodbye.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:49.790
Hey, Tachibana.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:52.420
Did you dump me because of him?

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.840
Don't think all men are like you!

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.410
Chikage and I are just childhood friends!

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:05.020
Chikage's mother was a resident housekeeper at my parents' house.

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:09.940
So we knew each other since grade school.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:12.200
Hey, Chikage.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:15.730
Aren't you in junior high? How can you not know simultaneous equations?

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:18.490
You need to be taught your homework by a grade school student?

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.400
D-Do you understand it?

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:21.770
Of course.

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:23.120
It's common knowledge.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:25.760
S-Sorry, young master.

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:31.410
Think about it this way. First you set the price of an apple and orange to X and Y.

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:32.920
Two apples and three oranges will be...

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.230
But when Chikage was in high school,
Two apples and three oranges will be...

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:35.910
But when Chikage was in high school,

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:38.330
his mother died.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:42.430
Chikage had no other relatives.

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:47.780
So my parents paid for him to go to college.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:54.230
Now he works for the Tachibanas to pay that back.

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:56.010
What a nice story.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:57.320
Is it?

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:58.780
The truth is...

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:02.920
At first, he worked as a secretary in one of my grandfather's companies, but...

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:03.890
But?
But?

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:08.170
He couldn't do any of the work, so they realized that a company job was out of the question.

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:10.790
So they hired him as a housekeeper.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:13.750
But he can't even do housework!

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:18.430
It's funny that he can't really do anything.

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:20.950
But isn't calling you "young master" strange?

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:22.730
It's like a period drama.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:28.110
Ooka Echizen was a long-running historical drama, set in 18th century Edo.
That's because we role-played "Ooka Echizen" when we were kids, and he just couldn't let it go.

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:30.370
Young master, that's not good.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.610
Don't say that, old man.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.180
But young master...

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.180
Young master!

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:38.640
This is a golden wafer filled with bean jam...

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:40.620
What the heck is that?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:45.370
I got out of my parents house and was enjoying living alone,

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.910
so why should I have to live with him?

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.000
Are you going to live with him?

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.580
I don't want to, but I think it'll end up that way.

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.140
I'm home.

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:56.630
Welcome home, young master.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:59.440
Would you like to take a bath, or would you like dinner first?

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:02.650
Oh! Let's bath together, since we haven't done that in a long time.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.650
Hey, Ono!

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:07.350
Weren't you thinking something strange right now?!

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:08.830
Umm... no...

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:11.480
Welcome.

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:14.800
What is it, sensei?

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:19.900
Let's do the preparations for tomorrow.

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:20.620
Right.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:26.700
Yes, three Presidents and one of each crème, correct?

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.490
Please wait a moment.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.570
Thank you very much.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:15.630
I thought Tachibana was the type of man that never let anyone, not just gays, get close to him.

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:19.130
Yet he can live with him.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.460
You're disgusting.

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.620
What's up, sensei?

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:26.430
Uh, nothing.

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:27.720
Oh?

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.140
Kanda-kun would you like to try this?

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:31.020
Are you sure?

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:32.600
Of course.

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:41.010
Is Chikage sleeping?

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:51.970
Young master.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:55.200
Young master.

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:00.620
What is it, Chikage?

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:02.980
Has everyone had lunch already?

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:04.830
Should I go buy something for you?

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:06.930
I-Is it already time for lunch?

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:07.540
Yes.

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:10.000
Well, don't just stand there.

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:11.650
First, get in here.

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:12.310
Yes.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:23.690
Oh, are you going to buy us lunch?

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:26.790
Yes. Please tell me what you'd like.

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:28.780
Then I want a hamburger.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.280
What about you, sensei?

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:32.740
I'm not your sensei...

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:34.660
Please don't be so reserved.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:38.860
Oh, then I want a Boston Café bagel sandwich with

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:41.360
mozzarella cheese and onions.

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:47.880
Is something wrong?

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:49.850
Your order won't work.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:51.840
It's too hard for Chikage.

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:53.720
I-I'm really sorry.

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:57.940
Then I'll go buy lunch for sensei.

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.080
I'm going.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:00.110
Then Chikage,

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:03.150
get me a tempura bowl with conger eel and vegetables from Hige-ten.

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:04.450
Yes, right away.

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:12.710
Somehow he seems happy to be able to do something for you.

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:14.010
You think so?

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:17.220
But it's really raining cats and dogs.

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:25.380
Hey, isn't it uncanny?

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:29.080
Yeah. It's raining as if someone upended a bucket of water on us.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:31.400
Didn't Eiji go on foot?

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:32.310
Yes.

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:37.200
Then I'll go get him in my car!

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:38.780
But if you're not here...

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:41.130
No customers will come in such a heavy rain.

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:42.970
Tachibana...

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:48.000
After all, he can be kind too.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:58.830
Umm...

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.760
What happened to you?

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:02.460
Didn't you take your car?

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.240
While I was shopping...

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:05.900
the car was...

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:08.150
What? Towed?

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:09.860
I'll go look for it again.

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:14.890
Are you all right?

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:18.100
S-Sorry.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:32.360
Encore.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.930
Damn it. He's absolutely my type.

00:15:40.930 --> 00:15:41.850
Umm...

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:44.070
N-No, it's nothing.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:45.300
Nothing.

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:47.150
Damn it.

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:51.230
I was only paying attention to the fact that he's Tachibana's childhood friend, so I didn't notice...

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:54.220
but he's absolutely the type I fall for.

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:56.900
Especially his face. It's unexpected.

00:15:56.900 --> 00:16:00.220
I totally love it! It's totally excellent.

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:02.680
It's really nice.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:03.520
No.

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:06.400
Oh, no! Don't come closer!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:08.980
I'm a devilish gay.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:10.940
Let me tell you how devilish I am...

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:13.330
Umm...

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.160
Are you really all right?

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:55.430
There.

00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:58.720
Doesn't it feel good?

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:16.350
I've done something wrong.

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:18.460
Sensei, are you all right?

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:22.800
By the way, why is it that the only person who didn't go anywhere is soaked to the skin?

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:26.830
I'll go change my clothes.

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:36.030
Why does it always happen like this?

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:41.010
It's insane that two men, both over thirty, would spin around together in the rain.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:49.960
But his face back then

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:51.380
was really nice.

00:18:56.270 --> 00:18:58.570
S-Sorry.

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:00.530
I didn't know what I was doing.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:05.390
Luckily, no one seems to have seen us, so I think we'd better go back inside.

00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:05.790
Umm...

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:07.250
Yes?

00:19:08.800 --> 00:19:10.870
M-May I ask your name?

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:20.280
Luckily, we didn't do anything yet.

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:23.510
I think he might get upset once he's calmed down.

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:26.180
It'll be okay.

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:36.500
U-Umm...

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:38.990
Th-Th-This...

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:48.050
I-It wasn't okay.

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:50.200
Th-Thank you.

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:54.050
Umm... If you don't mind, after work...

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:56.220
how about some tea at a family restaurant near here?

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:57.440
A family restaurant?

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:58.380
Yes.

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:01.960
Flowers, a restaurant...

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:05.510
For a man to take these steps is...

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:08.430
Fresh. To be honest, this hasn't happened to me before.

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:11.470
But, Chikage-san,

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:14.260
don't you have to go home with Tachibana?

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:18.380
No. I told him that I'd be back late tonight.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:20.420
I see...

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:23.730
Well... if it's only tea.

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:29.330
But the question is whether I'll be satisfied with such a pure relationship.

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:34.000
What if I did something with him

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.290
and Tachibana found out about it?

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:38.520
You're fired!

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:43.000
So...

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:45.220
it's not all right.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:49.850
What are you saying?

00:20:50.490 --> 00:20:52.050
Instead of tea...

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.660
let's go have a drink somewhere.

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:56.270
Sure.

00:20:56.750 --> 00:21:00.980
But don't tell Tachibana about this, okay?

